.TH PASTRY 1 "August 2026" "pastry 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pastry \- create and read pastebin.com pastes from the command line
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\fB<command> | pastry\fR [\fIoptions\fR]
\fBpastry\fR \fIurl-or-key\fR
\fBpastry list\fR [\fB-l\fR | \fB--limit\fR \fIN\fR]
\fBpastry delete\fR \fIurl-or-key\fR
\fBpastry whoami\fR
\fBpastry login\fR
\fBpastry logout\fR
\fBpastry --version\fR
\fBpastry --help\fR
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pastry
creates pastes from standard input and reads pastes to standard output. When
given a positional argument, it reads the paste identified by that key or URL.
When standard input is a pipe, it creates a paste.
.PP
Account operations (list, delete, whoami, private pastes) require a stored
API user key; run \fBpastry login\fR first.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-t, \-\-title \fIT\fR
Paste title.
.TP
.B \-f, \-\-format \fIF\fR
Syntax highlighting value (e.g. \fIgo\fR, \fIpython\fR).
.TP
.B \-e, \-\-expire \fIE\fR
Expiration: \fBN\fR, \fB10M\fR, \fB1H\fR, \fB1D\fR, \fB1W\fR, \fB2W\fR, \fB1M\fR, \fB6M\fR, or \fB1Y\fR.
.TP
.B \-g, \-\-guest
Force a guest paste (send no user key, even if logged in).
.TP
.B \-p, \-\-private
Make the paste private (requires login).
.TP
.B \-l, \-\-limit \fIN\fR
With \fBlist\fR, cap the number of pastes listed (1\-1000, default 50).
.TP
.B \-v, \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Print help and exit.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B list
List the logged-in user's pastes.
.TP
.B delete \fIurl-or-key\fR
Delete a paste owned by the logged-in user.
.TP
.B whoami
Show the logged-in user's account info.
.TP
.B login
Prompt for username and password and store the resulting API user key.
.TP
.B logout
Remove the stored API user key.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/pastry/config.json
Stores the pastebin API developer key and user key.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
\fBecho "hello" | pastry\fR
\fBecho "hi" | pastry --title greeting\fR
\fBpastry https://pastebin.com/AbC12345\fR
\fBpastry list\fR
\fBpastry delete AbC12345\fR
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
https://pastebin.com/doc_api
